        deviationFromMove: 11,
        intro: "Let's learn the modern Anti-Marshall slow Spanish: White plays **6.d3** instead of the classical **6.Re1**. The d3 setup defends **e4** with a pawn (rather than the rook), avoids the Marshall pawn-sacrifice complex entirely, and aims for a long manoeuvring middlegame. Magnus Carlsen has used this setup extensively at the world-championship level — it's the modern elite's preferred way to sidestep 25 moves of Marshall theory.",
